      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">15 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip ok\">Easy</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Sliding window - fixed size</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/maximum-average-subarray-i/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 643</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Maximum Average Subarray I</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Every window has the same length k, so the best average is the best sum divided by k. Keep a running sum of the last k elements: add the one entering, subtract the one leaving. O(n) time, O(1) space, one division at the end. It is the template for every fixed-size window question, and the base of the Hard follow-up \"length at least k\" (binary search on the answer).</p>\n"
  },
